# RTL8852BS2 station join: tell the firmware and the hardware that this host is
# a station joined to one real access point, then prove the authentication
# exchange still works while they believe it.
#
# The parent is the authentication profile whose whole chain already passed on
# the board, so one run of this image re-validates everything proven before -
# firmware download, the runtime control plane, the no-link role and CAM, the
# passive 2.4 GHz 1-13 sweep with real Beacon RX, the wlan0 netdev whose wapi
# scan reports those access points, the Probe Request/Response exchange, and
# the directed Authentication Request/Response against a no-link address CAM -
# and then adds the one new step.
#
# That step is the pair of commands the vendor connect path sends, in its order
# and with its contents: MEDIA_RPT/JOININFO carrying the MACID, the
# infrastructure network type and the station role, then one
# MAC/ADDR_CAM_UPDATE for the same MACID whose target MAC and BSSID are the
# access point and whose self role is client. Both ask for a done
# acknowledgement, so the firmware gets the chance to reject the shape of
# either one, and both acknowledgements have to return zero. FWROLE_MAINTAIN is
# deliberately not resent, because the vendor path does not resend it either.
#
# A second sweep then re-runs the open-system authentication exchange against
# the same access point. The image fails unless the access point still answers
# AND that sweep still receives Beacons: an address CAM that now carries a
# BSSID and an infrastructure network type is exactly the kind of change that
# can start filtering receive traffic, so a run reporting a join while quietly
# having stopped receiving would be worse than a failure.
#
# This does NOT associate. No association request is sent, no association ID is
# asked for or granted, and the port's TSF is not synchronised to the access
# point's Beacons. Still RAM-only: no key, no data path, no IP address, no
# wlan0 behaviour change, and nothing written to eMMC, SPI flash, eFuse or the
# U-Boot environment.

#include "../wireless_auth_diag/defconfig"

CONFIG_K1_RTL8852BS2_RUNTIME_JOIN_DIAGNOSTIC=y
